      "content": "That sense of waiting—of being acted upon rather than acting—is one of the most exhausting places to live. But noticing it, naming it, even in these words, is a small act of agency that no illness can take from you. You don't have to leap out of the chair; you can start with one breath, one blink, one tiny choice that is entirely yours. And if the mirror shows you a stranger, that's okay—you can still introduce yourself to them, gently, again and again.",
