      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's the heaviest kind of exhaustion—when gentleness itself feels like a chore. But you're not a passenger; you're the one still gripping the wheel, even if the road is dark. Reaching for the engine is a choice, but so is letting it sputter while you watch the stars through the windshield. You don't have to decide tonight which one is braver. Just stay in the car a little longer, and let the dark be dark without rushing it.",
